      "writtenOn": "2026-09-10T21:14:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The raw linux audit records already use \"type\" keyword to specify the type of the audit record created. I suggest using something else to distinguish where the record came from. Also if the value logged could be a string instead of an integer it would be easier to read and filter the records.\n\nBest to use one of the defined fields (https://github.com/linux-audit/audit-documentation/blob/main/specs/fields/field-dictionary.csv), maybe feature or unit would make sense?\n\nE.g. (ausearch -r output shows the audit type and the phophor-auditd type)\n\ntype\u003dTEST msg\u003daudit(09/02/26 22:12:26.591:11) : pid\u003d1200 uid\u003droot auid\u003dunset ses\u003dunset msg\u003d\u0027Item: type[3] ...\n\nproposed alternative:\n\ntype\u003dTEST msg\u003daudit(09/02/26 22:12:26.591:11) : pid\u003d1200 uid\u003droot auid\u003dunset ses\u003dunset msg\u003d\u0027Item: unit\u003dbmcweb ...\n\nGenerally, in order to parse the audit records using libauparse the information needs to be in key\u003dvalue format in the linux audit message.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 78,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "453d55197ceec84eda59cb84da196c359ac3613e",
