      "writtenOn": "2026-09-10T21:14:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m wondering about the vision of this configuration file. Would there be a single one for every service that wants to use the audit mechanism? Would every unique audit point need a command entry in the Allowlist in order to be logged? How will this scale for multiple services with multiple services and multiple audit entries?\n\n\nI\u0027m also wondering about the structure of the \"Allowlist\". Looks like it is service dependent? Can it be standardized? (I.e. define an event that is not necessarily tied to a particular service. Then include the event on the Allowlist for desired services, or more generally a global Allowlist for an event from any service?)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "453d55197ceec84eda59cb84da196c359ac3613e",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46b49a40_2e23dc31",
        "filename": "example/audit_daemon/audit.json",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000182
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T17:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Would there be a single one for every service that wants to use the audit mechanism?\n\nIn best case scenario - yes but planning two versions with precompiled headers which generated from json configs as hpp which will be included at compile time to targeted application and dbus as debug version.\n\n\u003e Would every unique audit point need a command entry in the Allowlist in order to be logged? \n\nUsually yes. Allowlist just a part of it, Denylist will work as exclude list.\n\n\u003e I\u0027m also wondering about the structure of the \"Allowlist\". Looks like it is service dependent?\n\nIt depends more on protocols than services but services usually attached to some protocol processing, so, yes, it is service dependant. As example, same hpp(with allowlist/denylist) file generated from json config could be attached to multiple services, so multiple services may send those audit entries to backend service.\nSame for dbus version, multiple services may use that allowlist/denylists.\n\n\u003e Can it be standardized?\n\nI\u0027d be glad to see it.",
      "parentUuid": "b4f874f6_bbecb4bc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "453d55197ceec84eda59cb84da196c359ac3613e",
